NAME-COLLISION DISPOSITION  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  This prompt's web source is features/vehicles/components/RecentActivity.tsx (the TWO-panel Recent Drives /
  Recent Charges feed). A DIFFERENT web component — features/dashboard/components/RecentActivity.tsx (feed +
  battery-trend chart + fleet-performance read) — shares the bare name "RecentActivity" and was already shipped
  by P-0130 into apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentActivity.* (11 files: .swift/.Types/.Adapter/.Model/
  .Views/.States/.Charts/.Previews/.Tests/.ModelTests/.strings). Both P-0130 and THIS P-0277 declare the IDENTICAL
  native output stem `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentActivity.*` — a genuine collision in the prompt
  set. Unlike 0237 AiUsageCard vs 0203 AIUsageCard (which differed by one letter's CASE and so could occupy two
  distinct stems), here the two component names are byte-identical, so the literal stem cannot host both.

  Resolution (the sanctioned "ship distinct, preserve predecessor, disclose" disposition): the VEHICLES surface
  ships under the `RecentActivity.Vehicles.*` stem (which still matches the prompt's allowed glob
  `RecentActivity.*`) with a `VehiclesRecentActivity` type prefix so the two surfaces compile side-by-side with
  ZERO symbol collisions. The 11 dashboard `RecentActivity.*` (P-0130) files are left BYTE-IDENTICAL —
  `git status --porcelain` over all 11 reports no change. The mandated P1/S11 telemetry slug is "RecentActivity"
  exactly as the prompt requires (`VehiclesRecentActivity.surfaceSlug`); it is shared conceptually with the
  dashboard surface (both are "Recent Activity"), which is an analytics-grouping choice, not a compile concern.

WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/vehicles/components/RecentActivity.tsx — props `drives: Drive[]?` + `sessions:
  ChargingSession[]?`, hooks `useTranslation` + `useUnits`. Two GlassPanels (web `grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2`):

    Recent Drives (FadeIn 0.25): header Route(cyan) + t('common.recentDrives','Recent Drives') + Link /drives
      t('common.viewAll','View all') + ChevronRight. drives.slice(0,5) → Link /drives/{id}: IconBox(cyan) Route;
      AnimatedNumber(convertDistanceFromSI(distance_m ?? 0, unitPrefs.distance), decimals 1, suffix ` {unit}`);
      TimeStamp(start_ts); InlineMetric(Clock, `${floor(duration_s/3600)}h ${fmtInt(floor((duration_s%3600)/60))}m`);
      if start_soc_pct!=null && end_soc_pct!=null → `{start}% → {end}%`. else t('common.noDrives','No drives recorded yet').
    Recent Charges (FadeIn 0.27): header BatteryCharging(emerald) + t('common.recentCharges','Recent Charges') +
      Link /charging viewAll. sessions.slice(0,5) → Link /charging/{id}: IconBox(green) Zap;
      AnimatedNumber(convertEnergyFromSI(total_energy_added_wh,'kWh'), decimals 1, suffix " kWh");
      TimeStamp(start_ts); InlineMetric(Clock, `${floor(duration_min/60)}h ${fmtInt(duration_min%60)}m`);
      if end_soc_pct!=null → `{start}% → {end}%`. else t('common.noCharges','No charging sessions recorded yet').
  Helpers (reproduced verbatim — arithmetic is the contract):
    fmtNumber(v,d)=safeNumber(v).toLocaleString(locale,{min/maxFractionDigits:d}); default precision 2, en-US,
      non-finite⇒0, half-away-from-zero; fmtInt(v)=fmtNumber(v,0);
    convertDistanceFromSI: km=m/1000 · mi=m/1609.344 · ft=m/0.3048;
    convertEnergyFromSI: kWh=wh/1000 · Wh=wh.
    Note: drive duration FLOORS the minutes BEFORE formatting; charge duration formats (rounds) the
    `duration_min % 60` remainder directly — both reproduced exactly, asserted by tests.
  i18n keys (5): common.recentDrives, common.recentCharges, common.viewAll, common.noDrives, common.noCharges.

