STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface)
  loading  → two skeleton panels (initial fetch, nothing resolved).
  content  → the two panels with up to five rows each.
  empty    → resolved with no drives AND no charges → BOTH panels still render, each with its own friendly empty
             message (web parity: panels never hidden). `phase == .empty` for telemetry/tests.
  error    → retryable error chrome (P4 leaf envelope; the web parent owns errors).
  stale    → header chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the live→stale transition.
  offline  → header chip + banner over last-known rows; no auto-refresh.

